# Rule 06. Text lives in content, not in templates

Language-agnostic. Zones and "literal text" are defined in rule 00. How a
template reads content in each stack is in the runtime appendix.

## Language

1. The default language is English. Demo data, fixtures and comments are English.
2. Other languages are separate content files, never code. No Cyrillic in
   code, comments or strings anywhere in `xgen`, `packages` and `apps`
   (`xgen check`, group `text`).

## Where text lives

| Text | Where |
| --- | --- |
| Interface text: titles, labels, buttons, menus, placeholders, empty states, screen-reader text | `xgen/content/ui/en.json`, generated into `@ui8kit/app-shared/content` as `ui`, read as `ui.group.key`; placeholders through `tpl()` |
| Demo records | the Codex fixtures in `xgen/fixtures` |
| Dev diagnostics (`throw new Error`, `console.*`) | code, English, never shown to users |

A block or a composite gets text through props filled by its parent, through
data, or from the `ui` dictionary. It never contains a sentence.

## What is literal text in composition

1. A text node with letters in a template: `<Text>Save</Text>`.
2. A string literal with letters in a text attribute or prop: `label`, `title`,
   `text`, `description`, `placeholder`, `hint`, `caption`, `heading`,
   `subtitle`, `message`, `summary`, `tooltip`, `alt`, `note`, `lead`, `legend`,
   `eyebrow`, `aria-label`, `aria-description`, `aria-placeholder`,
   `aria-roledescription`, `aria-valuetext` (and their PascalCase forms).
3. A string literal with letters as a result of a template expression:
   `{ok ? "Yes" : "No"}`.

## Allowed

- Technical values: `class`, `style`, `id`, `href`, `type`, `role`, `name`,
  `for`, `value`, `variant`, `size`, `tag`, `data-*`, routes, icon names.
- Strings with no letters: `/`, `·`, `—`, `12`, `…`.
- Anything that comes from a variable, a prop, a fixture or `ui.*`.

## Validation

`bun run check`, group `rules`, detector `literal-text`, scans the templates
of composition files. Script-level prose is reviewed, not checked.
Existing violations are in `rules/baselines/<package>.json`; the count may only go down.
